---
.title = "What you can depend on",
.description = "The checks behind glowcap's protocol, transports, bindings, and platforms.",
.date = .date("2026-07-25T00:00:00"),
.layout = "page.shtml",
.draft = false,
---

glowcap checks its protocol against the upstream OCapN suite and live
[Spritely Goblins](https://spritely.institute/goblins/) peers. Test coverage
varies by transport, language, and platform.

- `zig build check` runs in-process scenarios, committed wire fixtures,
  budgets, and public examples.
- Recurring live checks talk to the upstream OCapN suite and to a
  Goblins peer. A Chromium browser
  running the WebAssembly build also connects over a local secure WebSocket,
  and two Chromium Rooms members message each other over a WebRTC DataChannel.
  Full CI validation runs them.
- On-demand checks cover Tor and the full Goblins session over iroh. No check covers iroh across two separate NATs or a public
  certificate.

A live Goblins session proves protocol interop, not API stability. A live iroh
endpoint proves the transport stack, not agreement with another CapTP
implementation.

Check the [workflow results](https://github.com/glowcap-org/glowcap/actions/workflows/check.yml)
for the commit you plan to use. Development runs select jobs by changed
files, so a green run covers only those jobs. The
[repository stability guide](https://github.com/glowcap-org/glowcap/blob/main/docs/stability.md)
lists coverage and gaps for each area.
[Community review](https://github.com/glowcap-org/glowcap/blob/main/docs/community-review.md)
details the checks against OCapN and Goblins.

Use [Choosing a transport]($link.page('transports/choosing')) for deployment
tradeoffs and [Performance]($link.page('performance')) for measured costs. The
repository keeps the complete [feature
inventory](https://github.com/glowcap-org/glowcap/blob/main/docs/shipped.md) and
[known limitations](https://github.com/glowcap-org/glowcap/blob/main/docs/boundaries.md).
